{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157475-dark-eras-how-to-run-war-machines","id":1157475,"title":"[Dark Eras] How to run war machines?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-09T23:43:55-08:00","id":1157475,"title":"[Dark Eras] How to run war machines?","content":"So I found out we still needs some mechanics for <b>Dark Eras</b> metaline - exactly, war machines. My <b>Werewolf</b> players from Viking Age come to idea they can made <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballista\" target=\"_blank\">ballista</a> for their <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1137943-2e-fear-of-scales-%E2%80%93-dragon-idigam\">dragon hunting</a>. Now I wonder how to make it work mechanically - as ballista is, in practice <i>a very <b>big</b> </i>crossbow - to use it on dicepool take Dexterity + Archery / Firearms to roll. But how to gauge it's Damage level? Maybe in general CoD line ( like in <b>Armory</b> or <b>Hurt Locker</b> ) we have tank or missiles Damage ratings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-10-2017, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T00:13:53-08:00","id":1157477,"title":"","content":"I can tell you how it works in D&amp;D, maybe that's an inspiration: Basically, a ballista is a siege weapon that requires three (instant) actions to be operated: load, aim, fire. These can be performed by the same creature or multiple creatures, but must be performed in that order. Otherwise, a ballista functions like a normal weapon with an attack modifier and a damage dice pool equal to three times the damage of a heavy crossbow. Additionally, I believe a ballista has the Siege feature, meaning it deals double damage against structures but I'm not sure about that.<br /> <br /> For CofD, I'd consider using a similar system with a high damage rating. A crossbow has a rating of 2L in the rules revisions in Demon: the Descent. For a ballista, I'd adjudicate a damage rating, depending on its size. A crossbow has size 3, so a ballista could have damage equal to its Size-1 L. Human sized ballista? 4L. I'd probably just copy the load, aim, fire mechanism for the Ballista straight from D&amp;D, requiring 3 instant actions to operate the beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T01:22:44-08:00","id":1157479,"title":"","content":"<b>Dragotarify</b>, thanks for this idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I only points to this small small part...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragotarify</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157475-dark-eras-how-to-run-war-machines?p=1157477#post1157477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably just copy the load, aim, fire mechanism for the Ballista straight from D&amp;D, requiring 3 instant actions to operate the beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>So how to run this in game would be like this, I suppose:<ul><li><b><i>Load</i></b> needs large <i>Strength</i> - maybe 3, 4 dots? Half of balista<i> Size</i>? - and if not character meet this criteria, it needs to test on each turn it's <i>Strength</i>. On <i>Failure</i>, bolt goes out of his hands and need to repeat this action.</li> <li><b><i>Aim</i></b> is simple <i>Dexterity + Archery / Firearms</i> roll to hit thing - Question is should Defense or Armor apply to living beings? Like, my players just need 1 success with no penalties to hit dragon?</li> <li><i><b>Fire</b></i> is where I have the biggest problem now - So what, it's <i>Strength</i> test on operator? In Real Life it simply pulling the trigger once Aiming is done. Do not see testing here in very much....</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-10-2017, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T01:57:44-08:00","id":1157481,"title":"","content":"I prefer the simplified D&amp;D version of loading and aiming requiring no check, firing is a standard ranged attack (Dex + Firearms in CofD).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157475-dark-eras-how-to-run-war-machines?p=1157479#post1157479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So how to run this in game would be like this, I suppose:<ul><li><b><i>Load</i></b> needs large <i>Strength</i> - maybe 3, 4 dots? Half of balista<i> Size</i>? - and if not character meet this criteria, it needs to test on each turn it's <i>Strength</i>. On <i>Failure</i>, bolt goes out of his hands and need to repeat this action.</li> <li><b><i>Aim</i></b> is simple <i>Dexterity + Archery / Firearms</i> roll to hit thing - Question is should Defense or Armor apply to living beings? Like, my players just need 1 success with no penalties to hit dragon?</li> <li><i><b>Fire</b></i> is where I have the biggest problem now - So what, it's <i>Strength</i> test on operator? In Real Life it simply pulling the trigger once Aiming is done. Do not see testing here in very much....</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>With this level of mechanics, I think I'd go: Strength + Athletics for Loading, Wits + Firearms for aiming, Dexterity + Firearms for shooting. You basically split the &quot;aiming&quot; into two things. You could, of course, also just make it a two-action operation: Strength + Athletics for loading, Wits/Dexterity + Firearms for firing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T05:15:17-08:00","id":1157499,"title":"","content":"Other question I think about in this topic - <b>How much time should creation of balista and bolts take? </b>Building Equipment rules, from page 101 of <b>CoD</b> Rulebook states:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>To Roll or Not to Roll</b><br /> Building equipment should never take more than the time between one scene and the next. If it can\u2019t reasonably be built in a few hours or less, the character needs to acquire it another way. This system isn\u2019t meant to cover building a car from scratch or getting an entire business off the ground \u2014 it\u2019s for creating solutions to immediate problems. Building truly supernatural relics is beyond the capabilities of characters presented in this book.<br /> <br /> <b>If the character has plenty of time, isn\u2019t under any duress, and has dots in the relevant Skill equal to the equipment bonus a standard example of the equipment would provide, no roll is necessary. The Storyteller simply determines how long it should take and it\u2019s done, either with some roleplay within a scene, or it\u2019s stated to have happened between scenes.</b><br /> <br /> However, if the character is under pressure to get the job done before that werewolf picks up her scent, or while she\u2019s under attack by enormous slavering spiders, the player needs to roll. <b>Likewise, if she\u2019s trying to build something that\u2019s beyond her casual expertise (i.e., something with an equipment bonus greater than her dots in the relevant Skill, or some-thing the Storyteller determines is too complex to be made without a roll) then the dice come out. </b>The Storyteller may also call for a roll if the player wants to build a more impressive version of the equipment that has higher traits than the standard example. </div> </div> </div>I think that creating whole Balista should be about day work - but could needed to roll if character has less than Crafts 4 with it, because of Damage 4 it's attack do - but how much time would take to create one bolt? Assuming the character have needed wood that it is. Once scene - i.e. one hour - per bolt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-10-2017, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}